Review `wiring-07` complete. Report written to `docs/reviews/wiring/wiring-07-fluid-loop-port-wiring.md`.

**Key findings**: 7 total (2 high, 3 medium, 2 low). The two high-severity issues are:

1. **Fluid solver uses water cp (4186 J/kg·K) for all fluid types** — Glycol and refrigerant property differences are ignored in `FluidSolver::resolve` (`fluid_solver.rs:136`).
2. **Boiler supply temperature hardcodes `CP_LIQUID_WATER_J_KG_K`** — even when `fluid_type: Glycol` is configured (`boiler.rs:229, :522`).

Medium findings include: `PortSlots` silently splits same-loop different-fluid-type contributions, DHW port supply/return semantics are inverted vs hydronic convention, and no hydronic consumer model exists (boiler bypasses the fluid loop for zone heating).
